kosha vec-cross

  "vector-kriya vector-phala domain-math-sthita"
  "cross-product-abheda aayaama-traya-yukta"
  "vec-dot-pratipaksha"

  -- cross product of two 3D vectors: a × b
  -- [ax,ay,az] × [bx,by,bz] = [ay·bz - az·by, az·bx - ax·bz, ax·by - ay·bx]
  -- result is a vector perpendicular to both inputs
  -- magnitude = |a|·|b|·sin(θ) where θ is the angle between them
  -- direction: right-hand rule
  -- vec-dot gives scalar projection; vec-cross gives perpendicular direction
  -- together they are the two fundamental products in aayaama-traya
  --
  -- used in Rodrigues rotation (rot3d):
  --   v_rot = v·cosθ + (u × v)·sinθ + u·(u·v)·(1-cosθ)
  --   the cross product term gives the tangential component of rotation

shabda vec-cross / cross-product-of-two-3d-vectors-perpendicular-to-both

done
